{"kind":"artifact","text":"Candidate: the workroom UI tests at ui/test on exact head 311a1fa0fb828abcf3d1dd9920276b39ca663457. A mounted-render test now covers the work drawer's wiring to browser storage, which the suite could not see: the load happens in a mount effect and the save in a click handler, and both are invisible to the static renders in components.test.mjs. The new file seeds a Map-backed localStorage shim, mounts WorkView with no initialPersonalMemory so the component must reach storage itself, and follows a second topic by clicking. Severing the load makes it fail on the followed-topic assertion; severing the save makes it fail on the written-to-storage assertion, printing the unchanged stored value.","body":{"commit":"311a1fa0fb828abcf3d1dd9920276b39ca663457","path":"ui/test"}}